# Keeps the build context to actual sources.
#
# This is not only about speed. `COPY apps/api apps/api` would otherwise carry
# the HOST's `node_modules` and `dist` into the image, on top of the ones the
# build just produced — a Windows-built native module landing in a Debian
# container, and a stale `dist` silently shadowing the fresh one. The failure
# would appear at runtime, far from its cause.

node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
**/dist
**/.vite
**/coverage

.git
.github
.husky
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The web client is not part of the API image. Its manifest is copied
# explicitly by the Dockerfile — npm needs every workspace manifest to plan
# the tree — but none of its source or dependencies belong here.
apps/web/src
apps/web/public
apps/web/index.html
apps/web/vite.config.ts

docs
*.md
.docker-data
docker-compose.yml
